THIRD-PARTY DATA -- NOT DISTRIBUTED IN THIS REPOSITORY

The measured oscillating-aerofoil loops this work is compared with are
third-party experimental data. They were not produced by this work and are not
the author's to license, so they are not included here and LICENSE does not
extend to them. The original measurements are McCroskey, McAlister, Carr &
Pucci (1982), NASA TM-84245, a work of the U.S. Government; the digitised
frame files are obtained from L. Pancini, "BL-DSM-JFS-2021"
(https://github.com/luizpancini/BL-DSM-JFS-2021), which states no licence of its
own. The fetch script downloads them at run time into a git-ignored cache and
pins each file by SHA-256.

The University of Glasgow oscillating- and static-aerofoil runs used for the
second-facility test are likewise third-party data and are not included here.
They are: Green, R. B. and Giuni, M. (2017), "Dynamic stall database R and D
1570-AM-01: Final Report", University of Glasgow,
DOI: 10.5525/gla.researchdata.464, made available by its authors under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence. unistall/fetch_glasgow.py downloads
the runs at run time into the git-ignored cache and records a checksum of
each (data/glasgow_inventory.csv, data/glasgow_static_inventory.csv,
data/glasgow_sources.csv). The files in data/ and results/ whose names begin
with "glasgow_" are the author's own inventories and derived tables.

The static data files named static_naca0012_M030_*.csv are the author's own
digitisation of figures and tables in NASA TM-84245; each row names its source
page.
